// Renode platform description (.repl) for this board's MSS as the probe sees
// it. Start from the CPU and the console UART the probe prints on, then add
// each peripheral a probe touches. A device that only needs registers can be
// a `Memory` region or a tag; one that needs behaviour is a C# peripheral
// under peripherals/ referenced here.
//
// This is a starter: replace with the real board. The core is the project's
// choice (probes/toolchain.json, probes/_template/cpu.c); Renode's own
// platforms/cpus/*.repl show the CPU, interrupt controller and memory shape
// for each family. Example shape, with the board's names and addresses:
//
// cpu: CPU.<Family> @ sysbus
//     cpuType: "<core>"
//
// uart1: UART.<Model> @ sysbus <address>      the console the probe prints on
//
// flash: Memory.MappedMemory @ sysbus <address>
//     size: <bytes>
